# This file is kept for historical context, but is INTENTIONALLY empty.
#
# Gitleaks v8 (the version bundled with gitleaks/gitleaks-action@v3) only
# honors entries in .gitleaksignore that use the commit-fingerprint format:
#
#   <commit-sha>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>
#
# Plain-string allowlist entries are silently dropped (WR-01, Phase 70).
#
# The actual allowlist for the test-fixture secrets in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (test-jwt-secret-*, test-refresh-secret-*,
# test-encryption-key-*) lives in `.gitleaks.toml` under [allowlist].
#
# To suppress a real future finding, regenerate fingerprints with:
#   gitleaks detect --report-format json --report-path /tmp/leaks.json
#   jq -r '.[].Fingerprint' /tmp/leaks.json
# and append the resulting `<sha>:<file>:<rule>:<line>` lines here.
